<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duke Huan of Qi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 643 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duke Huan of Qi ruled the state of Qi in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from 685 to 643 BCE. With his minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guan-zhong">Guan Zhong</a> he reformed government and the economy and became the first of the hegemons of the Spring and Autumn period. He led alliances of states against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rong-people">Rong</a> and Di peoples and protected weaker states such as Xing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duke-huan-of-qi.jpg" alt="Duke Huan of Qi" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qihuangongguanzhong2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
